    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0517" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Mexico/411: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-02-29T12:00:00-06:00">February 29,
                            1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Referring to the Embassy’s despatch No. 3238, President today signed decree
                    designed to prevent alcohol smuggling which will appear in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Diario Oficial</hi> on Monday.<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d350-f1"/> Please notify the Treasury Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d350-f1" n="49" xml:id="d350-f1-content">
                <p>The Mexican decree was promulgated on March 9 and published in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Diario Oficial</hi> of March 12, entering into effect on
                    March 22.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
